{"__type":"$$EventMessageAiNode","id":"49a0e59e-e472-4581-9236-4d288faaa49a","ts":"2026-06-09T05:26:26.816-04:00","eventName":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","message":"n8n.ai.llm.generated","payload":{"executionId":"40","nodeName":"Model for LLM: Select Layouts","workflowName":"PPTX-Slides: Design Pipeline","nodeType":"@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatOpenAi","workflowId":"8LVqIvaDIEpH51yk","msg":"{\"messages\":[\"Human: Cho mỗi slide dưới đây, chọn layout phù hợp nhất.\\n\\nDanh sách layouts: cover, section-header, bullets, two-column, comparison, pros-cons, timeline, roadmap, stat-highlight, kpi-grid, quote, image-full, image-left, image-right, code, terminal, table, chart-placeholder, mindmap, pyramid, funnel, process-steps, checklist, team-grid, pricing, faq, demo, video-embed, closing, thank-you, contact\\n\\nSlides:\\nSlide 1: \\\"Giới thiệu tổng quan về chủ đề trình bày\\\" — - Chủ đề tập trung vào phát triển kinh tế số tại Việt Nam trong bối cảnh cách mạng công nghiệp 4.0.\\n...\\nSlide 2: \\\"Tầm quan trọng của chủ đề trong bối cảnh hiện tại\\\" — - Việt Nam đang đứng trước cơ hội lớn để vươn lên nhờ ứng dụng AI, IoT và blockchain.\\n- Chuyển đổi s...\\n\\nTrả về JSON array: [{\\\"slide_index\\\": 0, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"cover\\\"}, {\\\"slide_index\\\": 1, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"bullets\\\"}, ...]\"],\"options\":{\"openai_api_key\":{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"secret\",\"id\":[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]},\"model\":\"Qwen3-32B\",\"timeout\":60000,\"max_retries\":2,\"configuration\":{\"baseURL\":\"https://mkp-api.fptcloud.com/v1\",\"fetchOptions\":{}},\"model_kwargs\":{}},\"response\":{\"response\":{\"generations\":[[{\"text\":\"<think>\\nOkay, let's tackle this problem step by step. The user has provided a list of slides and a set of possible layouts for each. My task is to assign the most suitable layout to each slide based on its content. \\n\\nFirst, I'll need to understand each layout's typical use case. For example, \\\"cover\\\" is usually for the title slide, \\\"section-header\\\" for introducing a new section, \\\"bullets\\\" for lists of points, \\\"two-column\\\" for splitting content into two parts, etc. \\n\\nLooking at Slide 1: \\\"Giới thiệu tổng quan về chủ đề trình bày\\\" which translates to \\\"Overview of the presentation topic.\\\" The topic is about digital economy development in Vietnam in the context of Industry 4.0. Since this is the first slide, it's likely the title or cover slide. So \\\"cover\\\" seems appropriate here.\\n\\nSlide 2: \\\"Tầm quan trọng của chủ đề trong bối cảnh hiện tại\\\" meaning \\\"The importance of the topic in the current context.\\\" The content mentions opportunities for Vietnam using AI, IoT, blockchain, and mentions a transition. This slide probably lists several key points or reasons why the topic is important. The \\\"bullets\\\" layout is good for listing points, so that's a fit.\\n\\nI need to check if there are more slides, but the user only provided two examples. However, the instruction says to return a JSON array with all slides. Wait, the user provided two slides (Slide 1 and Slide 2) but the example response includes slide indices 0 and 1. Maybe they want me to assume that the slides continue, but since only two are given, perhaps I should just map those two. But the user might have more slides in their actual data. Hmm, maybe I should proceed with the given slides and structure the answer accordingly.\\n\\nWait, the user's input shows Slide 1 and Slide 2, but the example JSON has slide indices starting at 0. So Slide 1 would be index 0, Slide 2 index 1. That makes sense. \\n\\nSo for Slide 1 (index 0), \\\"cover\\\" is correct. Slide 2 (index 1) is a list of points explaining the importance, so \\\"bullets\\\". \\n\\nBut maybe there's a better layout for Slide 2? Let me think again. If the slide is about the importance, sometimes people use \\\"stat-highlight\\\" if they have key statistics, but the content here is more about points like AI, IoT, blockchain. \\\"Bullets\\\" is still the best fit. \\n\\nI don't see any other layout that would fit these slides better. So the JSON array would be [{\\\"slide_index\\\": 0, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"cover\\\"}, {\\\"slide_index\\\": 1, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"bullets\\\"}].\\n</think>\\n\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\\"slide_index\\\": 0, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"cover\\\"},\\n  {\\\"slide_index\\\": 1, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"bullets\\\"}\\n]\\n```\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":616,\"promptTokens\":240,\"totalTokens\":856}}}"}}
