s titled \\\"Định nghĩa và tầm quan trọng của Marketing số\\\". The content includes a definition and the importance of digital marketing. The bullet points start with \\\"Marketing số là việc sử dụng các nền tảng công nghệ để quảng bá sản phẩm/dịch vụ đến khách hàng.\\\" There's an ellipsis, so maybe more points follow. Since this is an introductory slide explaining what digital marketing is and its significance, the best layout would be one that can present a title with a few bullet points. The 'bullets' layout is designed for this purpose. Alternatively, if there were a lot of text or a focus on a single key point, maybe 'section-header', but since it's a definition and some points, 'bullets' seems right. The 'cover' layout is typically for the title slide, which might have a larger title and maybe an image, but here Slide 1 is the first content slide, not the cover. So Slide 1 should be 'bullets'.\\n\\nSlide 2 is titled \\\"Sự khác biệt và các kênh Marketing số phổ biến\\\". The content starts with \\\"Khác biệt: Marketing truyền thống tập trung vào phương tiện như TV, báo chí; Marketing số dựa trên...\\\" and mentions common digital marketing channels. This slide is comparing traditional vs. digital marketing and listing channels. The 'comparison' layout is designed for showing differences between two items, which fits the first part. However, if there are multiple points or a list of channels, maybe 'bullets' again. But since the title mentions both difference and common channels, perhaps the first part is a comparison and the second part is a list. The 'comparison' layout could work for the first part, but the second part (channels) might need a different approach. Alternatively, 'two-column' could split the slide into two parts: one for differences and one for channels. But the 'comparison' layout is more specific for contrasting two entities. So I think 'comparison' is suitable here because the primary focus is on the differences between traditional and digital marketing, and the channels can be listed in the same layout or maybe as bullet points under each column. \\n\\nWait, the available layouts include 'comparison', which is for showing side-by-side comparisons. So if the slide is about differences between traditional and digital marketing, using 'comparison' makes sense. But the second part also lists common channels. Maybe the slide has two sections: one comparing the two types and another listing the channels. If that's the case, perhaps 'bullets' again, but the initial part is a comparison. Hmm. The user might expect the layout to match the main purpose. Since the title includes \\\"Sự khác biệt\\\", the comparison layout is appropriate for that part. The rest of the content could be additional bullet points, but the primary layout choice is based on the main content. So I'll go with 'comparison' for Slide 2.\\n\\nNow, checking the list of layouts again to make sure I didn't miss anything. 'Two-column' is for splitting content into two columns, which could be used if there are two separate lists. But 'comparison' is more structured for contrasting two sides. So yes, 'comparison' is better here.\\n\\nSo the final answer should be Slide 1: 'bullets', Slide 2: 'comparison'. Let me verify once more. Slide 1 is a definition and points, so bullets. Slide 2 is comparing two marketing types and listing channels. The comparison layout can handle the contrast, and maybe the channels can be in a list within that layout. Alternatively, if the channels are a separate section, maybe 'bullets' again, but the title emphasizes the difference, so 'comparison' is the best fit.\\n</think>\\n\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\\"slide_index\\\": 0, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"bullets\\\"},\\n  {\\\"slide_index\\\": 1, \\\"layout\\\": \\\"comparison\\\"}\\n]\\n```\",\"generationInfo\":{\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}}]]},\"tokenUsage\":{\"completionTokens\":880,\"promptTokens\":232,\"totalTokens\":1112}}}"}}
